<title>PHILIPPINES: Island Mining converts to holding firm.</title>
<headline>Island Mining converts to holding firm.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine firm Island Mining &amp; Industrial Corp said on Friday it had been converted into a holding and investments company.</p>
<p>In a notice to the Philippine Stock Exchange, the company said its stockholders approved on Sept 11, the change in company name to Island Resources &amp; Holdings Corp.</p>
<p>Island Mining also withdrew its application with the Securities and Exchange Commission for a capital hike from 50 million to 70 million pesos. It did not give a reason for the withdrawal of the application.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
